{
  "title": "High Tibial Osteotomy",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/recon/3135/high-tibial-osteotomy",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Apr 26 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "High Tibial Osteotomy (HTO) is a surgical procedure that is performed to correct angular deformities of the knee to prevent development or progression of unicompartmental osteoarthritis.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "It is predominately done to correct for varus deformities in young patients but can also be done to correct valgus deformities.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Contraindications include inflammatory arthritis, flexion contracture > 15 degrees, bicompartmental osteoarthritis, and ligamentous instability.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Primary or secondary medial knee arthrosis is the most common indication",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Isolated lateral compartment osteoarthritis is much less common",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Use",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "predominately done for **varus deformities**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**less common for valgus deformities**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Angular deformity in the knee leads to abnormal distribution of weight bearing stresses",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "can **accelerate wear in medial or lateral compartments** of the knee and lead to degeneration",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**HTO is commonly combined with cartilage restoration procedures** to provide better mechanical environment for biologic repair",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Mechanical axis of lower extremity",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "can be assessed by drawing straight line from **center of femoral head to the center of the ankle joint**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "line axis should pass just **medial to the medial tibial spine**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Varus vs Valgus alignment",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain on medial or lateral side of knee",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "knee malalignment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3135/images/varusknee.jpg",
                  "caption": "varus"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "standing alignment hip-to-ankle films",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "show knee malalignment using mechanical axis line",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Studies",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Indications",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "young, active patient (<50 years) in whom an arthroplasty would fail due to excessive wear",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "healthy patient with **good vascular status**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "non-obese patients",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "pain and disability interfering with daily life",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "only one knee compartment is affected",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "compliant patient that will be able to follow postop protocol",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "General contraindications",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inflammatory arthritis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**obese patient BMI>35**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**flexion contracture >15 degrees**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**knee flexion <90 degrees**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "procedure will need >20 degrees of correction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "patellofemoral arthritis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "ligament instability",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**varus thrust during gait**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Valgus-producing tibial osteotomy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Goals",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "unload the involved joint compartment by correcting tibial malalignment",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "A medial unloader brace can be used for therapeutic and diagnostic purposes. If a patient benefits from the brace, they are likely to benefit from surgery.",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "maintain the joint line perpendicular to mechanical axis of the leg",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "can be done for varus knee with medial compartment degeneration (more common)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**best results achieved by overcorrection of the anatomical axis to 8-10 degrees of valgus**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Contraindications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "narrow lateral compartment cartilage space with stress radiographs",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "loss of lateral meniscus",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "lateral tibial subluxation >1cm",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "medial compartment bone loss >2-3mm",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "varus deformity >10 degrees",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Varus-producing tibial osteotomy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Used less commonly than distal femoral osteotomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "produces obliquity of the tibiofemoral joint line",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Goals",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "unload the involved joint compartment by correcting tibial malalignment",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "maintain the joint line perpendicular to mechanical axis of the leg",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "can be done for valgus knee with lateral compartment degeneration",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "deformity should be **<12 degrees or else the joint line will become oblique**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Contraindications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "medial compartment arthritis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "loss of medial meniscus",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "distal femoral osteotomy better if lateral femoral condyle hypoplasia present",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "adjunct to soft tissue reconstructive surgeries (ACL/PCL/MACI) when there is coronal malalignment",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technique",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Lateral closing wedge technique**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3135/images/closingwedge.jpg",
              "caption": "closing wegdge"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "wedge of bone removed with tibia via an anterolateral approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "ORIF of wedge",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "has advantages",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "more inherent stability allows for faster rehab and weight bearing",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "no required bone grafting",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Medial opening wedge technique**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3135/images/openingwedge.jpg",
              "caption": "opening wedge"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "transverse bone cut made in proximal tibia, and wedged open on medial side",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "ORIF of wedge",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "has advantages",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**of maintaining posterior slope**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "increasing slope increases stress on ACL, while decreased slope alleviates stress on the ACL",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "avoids proximal tibiofibular joint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "avoids peroneal nerve in anterior compartment",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Focal dome osteotomy** (concavity proximal)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "the center of the dome is located at the center of rotation of angulation (CORA)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "has advantages",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "corrects limb alignment with the least translation of bone ends",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "least translation of anatomical axis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "minimal shortening",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Recurrence of deformity**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "60% failure rate after 3 years when",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "failure to overcorrect",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "patients are overweight",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Loss of posterior slope**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Patella baja**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3135/images/patellabaja_small_moved.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "refers to a shortened patellar tendon which decreases the distance of the patellar tendon from the inferior joint line",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "can be caused by **raising tibiofemoral joint line in opening wedge osteotomies**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "can be caused by **retropatellar scarring and tendon contracture**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "can cause bony impingement of patella on tibia",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Compartment syndrome**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Peroneal nerve palsy**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "more common in lateral opening wedge osteotomy and lateral closing wedge osteotomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "minimal risk in medial opening wedge osteotomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Malunion or nonunion**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Varus-producing high tibial osteotomy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "success rate is 87% in 10 years",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Valgus-producing high tibial osteotomy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "success rate is 50-85% in 10 years",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Good clincial results with later conversion to total knee athroplasty",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
